 12pt'><u><strong>Vaccines given in special circumstances:</strong></u></span></p>\n<div class=\"mm-table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"mm-table\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;\"><colgroup><col style=\"width:84.45pt;\"><col style=\"width:167.05pt;\"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Vaccines</p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Indications</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Hep A</p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18pt;margin-bottom:8pt;\">1.  Long term liver disease.</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;\"><li data-source-marker-codepoints=\"U+0025 U+0031 U+002E\"><span class=\"list-prefix\" style=\"display:inline-flex;width:18pt;\"><span class=\"list-marker\">1.</span><span class=\"list-tab\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-list-suffix=\"tab\" style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;\"></span></span>Hemophilia.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints=\"U+0025 U+0031 U+002E\"><span class=\"list-prefix\" style=\"display:inline-flex;width:18pt;\"><span class=\"list-marker\">2.</span><span class=\"list-tab\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-list-suffix=\"tab\" style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;\"></span></span>Poor sanitary condition.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints=\"U+0025 U+0031 U+002E\"><span class=\"list-prefix\" style=\"display:inline-flex;width:18pt;\"><span class=\"list-marker\">3.</span><span class=\"list-tab\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-list-suffix=\"tab\" style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;\"></span></span>Living near to sewage.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints=\"U+0025 U+0031 U+002E\"><span class=\"list-prefix\" style=\"display:inline-flex;width:18pt;\"><span class=\"list-marker\">4.</span><span class=\"list-tab\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-list-suffix=\"tab\" style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;\"></span></span>Living with primates.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints=\"U+0025 U+0031 U+002E\"><span class=\"list-prefix\" style=\"display:inline-flex;width:18pt;\"><span class=\"list-marker\">5.</span><span class=\"list-tab\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-list-suffix=\"tab\" style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;\"></span></span>Drug abusers.</li></ol></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Hep B</p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">1. Sex workers.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">2. Living with Hep B positive.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">3. Drug abusers.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">4. Multiple sex partners.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">5. Regular transfusions.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">6. Liver disease or CKD.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">7. Travelling to endemic areas.</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Meningococcal </p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">1. Asplenia.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">2. Immune suppression.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">3. Complement deficiency.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">4. High risk endemics travel.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">5. University students &lt; 25 years of age</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">6. Contact with infected individuals.</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Pneumococcal</p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">1. Asplenia.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">2. SCD.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">3. Splenectomy.</p><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">4. HIV.</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Typhoid </p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">1. Travel to endemics.</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Rabies</p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">- Post exposure prophylaxis recommended</p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">- Pre \u2013 exposure prophylaxis \u2013 where risk of exposure to rabies is substantial.</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\"></p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">Yellow fever</p></td><td style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;\"><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">- High case fatality.</p><p style=\"margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;\">- Given when travel is un avoidable.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19177]\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Breast Feeding:</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt